======================================================================
QUESTION REQUIREMENTS
======================================================================

Include exactly THREE or FOUR numbered questions.

Each question should include a bold mini-title.

Questions should build naturally.

Typical progression

Question 1

Perform the primary mathematical task.

Question 2

Extend or represent the mathematics.

Whenever appropriate, combine computation and interpretation into the SAME question rather than separating them.

Question 3

Interpret the result in the context of the scenario.

Question 4 (optional)

Make a recommendation, prediction, engineering decision, business decision, or explain the long-term behavior.

The final question should always return to the original scenario.

The mathematical tasks should follow the approach suggested by question.txt and verified_answer.txt.

======================================================================
ANSWER KEY REQUIREMENTS
======================================================================

Include

\section*{Answer Key}

Keep the answer key concise.

For each question include

• Final answer
• Brief explanation

Do NOT include lengthy derivations unless absolutely necessary.

The explanations should closely follow the reasoning and approach used in verified_answer.txt while being rewritten to match the new scenario.

